<title>UK: Reckitt up on outlook, Natwest upgrade.</title>
<headline>Reckitt up on outlook, Natwest upgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Reckitt &amp; Colman gained ground on Wednesday after the company said it expected the momentum of 1996 to continue this year.</p>
<p>At 1140 GMT, the shares were trading 8-1/2p higher at 897-1/2, testing the all-time intraday high at 905 set on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The UK household products group told shareholders at its annual meeting that its performance remained robust.</p>
<p>NatWest markets upgraded the stock to &quot;buy&quot; from &quot;hold,&quot; which also bolstered the shares, dealers said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
